  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its design, bulk, mass, scale and siting, would appear incongruous and out of keeping with the prevailing character of the host dwelling, the terrace row, and the distinctiveness and historic character of the Becontree Estate. The proposal would result in a detrimental loss of symmetry across the terrace row, a disruption to the planned form of the Estate,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the loss of the open aspect to the corner plot. It would thereby cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the area, including to the historic distinctiveness of the Becontree Estate. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness: National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
